# Destructive filesystem guard

**Incident (binding):** 2026-08-15 · lead-dev G0 hygiene intended to delete a chrome profile. PowerShell `cmd /c "rmdir /s /q \"E:\...\"` lost the quotes and ran `rmdir /s /q \` against **drive E:\**. Recycle Bin, OneDrive, Viewer worktrees, `.git`, and artifact stores were walked.

Hygiene is **not** a license to recursive-delete. Same machine, same risk in this repo.

## Never run

```text
cmd /c rmdir /s
rmdir /s /q
Remove-Item -Recurse   on anything other than one resolved leaf
robocopy ... /MIR
git clean -fdx
del /s /q
rm -rf
```

Never pass a filesystem path through `cmd /c` with escaped quotes (`\"...\"`). Use PowerShell `-LiteralPath` only.

## Allowed delete (all must hold)

1. Target is **one** existing leaf (file or empty-enough directory).
2. `Resolve-Path -LiteralPath` succeeds.
3. Resolved full path **starts with** an allowlist prefix written in the WAVE_CARD / this turn's task.
4. Resolved path does **not** equal and does **not** prefix-match a deny prefix.
5. After delete, confirm the allowlist parent still contains `.git` when it existed before.

If any check fails: **do not delete**. Leave the folder. Gitignore it. Write a pointer note. STOP.

## Deny prefixes (abort immediately)

```text
E:\
C:\
E:\$RECYCLE.BIN
C:\$Recycle.Bin
E:\0-Development\
E:\0-Development\Dashboard\
E:\0-Development\Viewer\
E:\OneDrive*
C:\Users\
**/.git
**/apps
**/src
**/packages
**/node_modules
```

Also abort if command output contains: `$RECYCLE.BIN` · `pagefile.sys` · `Program Files` · `System Volume Information` · `OneDrive`.

## Chrome / browser profiles

Do **not** recursive-delete `**/.chrome-profile*` or `**/chrome-profile*` under the repo or evidence. Options:

- leave in place (gitignored)
- `Move-Item -LiteralPath` to a **new** gitignored scratch **outside** the repo, destination created first and verified

Never `robocopy /MIR` an empty dir onto a profile path.

## Orchestrator / strategy

Do not put “recursive delete chrome profile / free disk / wipe scratch” in a WAVE_CARD or TEAM_DIRECTIVE. Full-auto does not include drive hygiene.
